WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.810
The second Purge movie takes place 1 year
after the original and unemployment has risen

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.040
from 1% in the previous movie to 5%.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.730
This may be a reflection of the economy in
the world of The Purge worsening, despite

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.990
the claims by the political group, The New
Founding Fathers of America, that The Purge

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.060
benefits the economy.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:18.269
As we now know first hand, it turns out massive
amounts of death actually isn’t so great

00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:22.010
for the economy as a whole, save for a select
few of the world’s wealthiest companies.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.950
In our world, Walmart and Amazon are the rare
examples of thriving businesses, but in the

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.840
world of the Purge it’s all about weapon
manufacturers.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.650
This all plays into the commentary that Anarchy
makes about gun violence in the US.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:36.680
To learn the true meaning behind everything
that happens in Anarchy, including how Universal

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.971
took a SHOT at a rival film studio, stick
around to the end of this video.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:46.990
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:52.260
The first pur… the original Purge introduced
the New Founding Fathers, so this time around

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.710
we learn a little bit more about them and
we meet their opposition, a revolutionary

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.850
group headed up by Carmelo Johns.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:01.690
Johns surmises that the Purge is a tool to
funnel money upward to the upper class: the

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:03.240
politicians and their rich donors.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.120
It is the poor who are most likely to die
on Purge night, as they are unable to protect

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.120
themselves.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:12.009
This makes it appear as if the NFFA is doing
a great job by cleaning up the streets and

00:01:12.009 --> 00:01:15.280
reducing the taxes that go towards welfare
to take care of those people.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.700
Those rich political donors that I mentioned
likely consist of two groups, those who sell

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.210
security, as we saw in the previous movie,
and those who sell weapons, which we start

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:24.408
to see in this movie.

00:01:24.408 --> 00:01:27.498
Everyone wants to get in on the so-called
“holiday” sales trend.

00:01:27.498 --> 00:01:31.569
Even the street vendors try to sell Eva weapons
as she walks home, telling her she needs them

00:01:31.569 --> 00:01:35.310
as “protection” as casually as tourist
shops might tell vacationers that they need

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:38.013
an item to commemorate their trip, and these
are the same stalls that

00:01:38.013 --> 00:01:40.889
you might find in LA selling t-shirts and postcards.

00:01:40.889 --> 00:01:45.509
The use of The Purge as a money making tool
in 2023 is really only a slight exaggeration

00:01:45.509 --> 00:01:49.979
of what goes on in real life, where organizations
like the NRA donate tens of millions of dollars

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:54.259
per year to fund election campaigns for politicians
who will do what they say, so when these weapons

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:58.119
are used for the inevitable act of terror,
the gun companies can rest assured that their

00:01:58.119 --> 00:02:00.710
politicians won’t do anything to hurt their
weapon sales.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:04.670
The satirization of American gun culture is
a thread that runs through the entire movie,

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:08.369
and seemingly the rest of the series, but
there are also other themes, and connections

00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:09.409
you might not have noticed.

00:02:09.409 --> 00:02:10.775
Let’s get into the Things You Missed.

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:19.939
During the opening title, we see the seal
of The New Founding Fathers of America.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:23.650
It’s very reminiscent of the Great Seal
of the United States, the differences being

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:28.099
that in the NFFA seal, the eagle is holding
an assault rifle and machete instead of arrows

00:02:28.099 --> 00:02:29.239
and an olive branch.

00:02:29.239 --> 00:02:33.790
The wings are much more rigid, like jet wings
and the glory of stars, which originally represented

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:37.760
the 13 American colonies coming together,
is thoughtfully replaced with two knifes coming

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.099
together -- a symbol of unification replaced
with a symbol of conflict.

00:02:41.099 --> 00:02:45.480
The first character we meet is Eva, a waitress
taking care of a customer named Mr. Sabian.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.069
“How is everything Mr. Sabian?”

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:49.049
"Great as always."

00:02:49.049 --> 00:02:53.209
Sabian is a name that director James Demonaco
often includes in his movies as a director’s

00:02:53.209 --> 00:02:56.730
trademark, but it has special meaning in The
Purge franchise, where it is often tied to

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.329
a character with some kind of link to the
NFFA.

00:02:59.329 --> 00:03:02.950
In The Purge, Mr. Sabian was one of the neighbors
who went hunting during The Purge and in the

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:06.989
prequel, The First Purge, Arlo Sabian is the
NFFA Chief of Staff.

00:03:06.989 --> 00:03:09.890
This time, Mr. Sabian is played by an actor
named Vick Sabian.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:12.030
There’s another potential reference on the
TV.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:15.700
The news scroller at one point reads: “A
drive along Oregon’s coast reveals soaring

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:19.680
sand dunes,” which may be a nod to the production
company, Platinum Dunes.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.329
The news anchor also says that more people
will partake in this Purge than ever before.

00:03:23.329 --> 00:03:26.959
I mentioned in the last episode that this
is the case in seemingly every Purge that

00:03:26.959 --> 00:03:29.219
we’ve seen, and in Anarchy we find out why.

00:03:29.219 --> 00:03:30.219
Roll it.

00:03:30.688 --> 00:03:32.340
“Tonight we take lives.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.879
We make things manageable for us.

00:03:35.879 --> 00:03:38.393
Unfortunately, the citizens aren’t killing
enough.

00:03:38.393 --> 00:03:40.187
So we supplement it all.

00:03:40.187 --> 00:03:42.740
To keep things balanced.”

00:03:43.209 --> 00:03:47.239
As commencement draws closer a married couple,
Shane and Liz rush to get to shelter and see

00:03:47.239 --> 00:03:51.349
people putting out blue baptisias, which the
previous movie explains to be a sign of support

00:03:51.349 --> 00:03:52.349
for the Purge.

00:03:52.349 --> 00:03:55.359
We don’t see them as much as you would expect in this movie, which may be because of a shortage

00:03:55.359 --> 00:03:58.769
caused by a drought, as explained in an article
on the NFFA website.

00:03:58.769 --> 00:04:03.129
You can also spot men putting up plywood,
and this shot is a powerful visual representation

00:04:03.129 --> 00:04:06.790
of what Carmelo Johns preaches about the poor
being the ones who suffer most during The

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:11.090
Purge, while the NFFA can afford to sit back
behind their high tech security systems.

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:14.620
While Eva is walking home, you can get a slight
glimpse of a poster advertising the suspension

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:18.280
of emergency services during The Purge, which
is actually just a movie poster from the ad

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.930
campaign of the original movie.

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:24.300
In that film, we encountered one group of
Purgers that wore creepy, nondescript masks.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.294
Shane and Liz encounter a new group who travel
around on motorbikes, skateboards and a large

00:04:28.294 --> 00:04:28.991
van.

00:04:28.991 --> 00:04:32.000
Some of them have religious iconography on
their masks or faces.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.870
The last movie did have a little bit of evidence
of The Purge starting to become a religion,

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:39.350
with the crazy neighbors holding hands and
reciting something like a prayer, the emergency

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:43.580
broadcast ending with this:
“...blessed be our New Founding Fathers

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.650
and America, a nation reborn”

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:49.710
...and maybe even the choice of flowers, the
blue baptisias, being a reference to baptism,

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:52.699
the symbolic form of purification in some
religions.

00:04:52.699 --> 00:04:56.541
It goes along nicely with a phrase commonly
chanted by purgers: 

00:04:56.811 --> 00:04:58.811
"Purge and Purify!

00:04:59.123 --> 00:05:00.377
Say it with me."

00:05:00.497 --> 00:05:02.497
"Purge and Purify!"

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.750
Anarchy takes the religious parallels the
next level.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:09.180
I think the idea is that by making the violence
into a religious experience, the NFFA hopes

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:13.050
people will look past their morals, and blindly
accept it as an OK thing to do.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:16.360
Many people follow religion to help guide
their morality, but I’m sure you can also

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:20.860
think of examples of those who use their religion
as an excuse to justify horrible behaviour.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.960
Like those nutcases who try to ban horror
movies.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.643
Those people have strayed SO FAR from the
light.

00:05:25.851 --> 00:05:27.851
"Purge and Purify!"

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:31.520
We see The Purge become more and more intertwined
with religion throughout the first three Purge

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:32.020
movies.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.212
Carmelo calls this out in one of his rants.

00:05:35.099 --> 00:05:40.630
“We no longer worship at the altar of Christ,
Mohammed, Yahweh.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:43.539
We worship at the altar of Smith and Wesson.”

00:05:43.539 --> 00:05:45.889
Smith and Wesson is a firearm manufacturer.

00:05:45.889 --> 00:05:48.310
Next is the sniper woman acting as a herald
from a rooftop.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:50.800
Her speech is rife with religious entitlement.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.669
She says: “I'm doing God's work.

00:05:52.669 --> 00:05:54.470
He uses an earthquake, a virus.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:55.980
The masses nourish and flourish.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:57.580
I am that virus tonight.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.800
I am a one-woman f***ing plague and you're
all in my path!

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.009
I am the Holy Trinity.

00:06:02.009 --> 00:06:04.850
I am the Father F***er, Son of a B****, and
Holy S***!

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:07.080
And my MP-9 silver-tipped Auto Magnum.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.919
The right arm of the free world and the left
hand of God!

00:06:09.919 --> 00:06:13.379
In flaming fire, I take the heads of them
that know not God.”

00:06:13.379 --> 00:06:16.910
And the host of the Purge Gala at the end
of the movie describes one the weapons that

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.530
she considers her favorite.

00:06:19.414 --> 00:06:25.684
“It is so precise it’s as if God had crafted
it himself.”

00:06:25.684 --> 00:06:27.980
That brings me to the Purge countdown billboard.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:32.322
When hacked by Carmelo’s group, it glitches
out and momentarily reveals a hidden message.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:46.199
Probably the most iconic new villain in this
second Purge movie is this guy, who for obvious

00:06:46.199 --> 00:06:47.940
reasons, I’ll just call “Godhead.”

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:52.240
It seems that he’s labeling himself as God,
a decider of who lives and who dies.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.300
Halfway through the annual Purge, Carmelo’s
revolutionary group taps into the video feed

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:59.909
of the countdown to deliver a message to the
people about the NFFA.

00:06:59.909 --> 00:07:03.850
His video contains a lot of distortion and
visual glitches which seems to be purely for

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:05.030
aesthetic purposes.

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:08.820
One of the glitches shows New Founding Father
Donald Talbot, and if we pause right as it

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:12.690
happens, the word EVIL is written across his
forehead in the same spot Godhead has written

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:13.690
the word God.

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:17.490
Other subliminal messages in this presentation
include a message reading: Frick the Purge

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:20.210
and a protest sign that says Where Corruption
Begins.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:24.580
WCB may stand for Workers Compensation Board,
the state agency that provides benefits to

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.139
those that get injured during work.

00:07:26.139 --> 00:07:29.660
We never hear anything more about this, but
based on what we do know, it’s not hard

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:33.030
to come to the conclusion that the NFFA is
using the Purge to take out people that were

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:35.509
injured on the job so that they don’t have
to pay them.

00:07:35.509 --> 00:07:40.160
This would be yet another example of The Purge
disproportionately affecting the working class.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.160
Speaking of which...

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.099
LIZ: “You know, we don’t have a lot of time
before commencement, Shane.”

00:07:44.099 --> 00:07:45.490
SHANE: “We’ll be fine.

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:46.490
I promise.”

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:47.770
He would not be fine.

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:50.110
The last character we meet is Leo Barnes.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:53.430
These articles on his wall tell us he’s
the new Jeff Denlon and if you look closely,

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:57.240
you’ll notice the drunk driver who hit his
son was let off the hook just two weeks ago,

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.680
around the same time that Leo would have disabled
the man’s security system.

00:08:01.301 --> 00:08:04.466
“Two weeks ago I came here and disabled
his back barricade, that’s what we’re

00:08:04.466 --> 00:08:05.369
doing here.”

00:08:05.369 --> 00:08:09.610
By the way, we spend most of the movie wondering
how Barnes got all his awesome combat skills.

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:12.810
When he drives out of the garage, it looks
like he’s got a cop car with extra metal

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:13.889
armor covering the body.

00:08:13.889 --> 00:08:17.330
Then when he comes face to face with this
guy at the end, he says they looked up his

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.129
info, and he refers to him “sergeant”.

00:08:19.129 --> 00:08:22.979
So it seems like Barnes learned to kick ***
because he used to be a police sergeant.

00:08:22.979 --> 00:08:25.879
When The Purge is about to begin, Shane is
still optimistic.

00:08:26.569 --> 00:08:28.760
“Hey hey hey. Don't worry.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.190
We’ll figure something out.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:30.928
I promise.”

00:08:30.928 --> 00:08:31.983
Promise.

00:08:31.983 --> 00:08:34.299
I do not think he knows what that word means.

00:08:34.299 --> 00:08:37.950
Speaking of which, when Eva and her daughter
Cali have their apartment invaded by the sweaty

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.390
guy from their building, he seems a little
confused on the name of his favorite government

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:43.490
tyrants, calling them the New Found Fathers.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:45.180
“It’s my right!

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:49.002
Granted to me by the New Found Fathers.”

00:08:49.002 --> 00:08:53.290
Maybe he was confusing them with a certain
late 90s early 2000s pop-punk act, but I just

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:56.690
had to point this out, because it seems to
have predicted this whole 2020 phenomenon

00:08:56.690 --> 00:09:00.070
known as the “Karen meme”, where these
people film someone breaking the rules, and

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:03.360
the person freaks out and claims they have
the right to do whatever it is they’re doing

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:06.110
and usually cites made up information and
makes a huge scene.

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:10.108
“I’m going to get my order, and I have
a right.”

00:09:10.108 --> 00:09:13.690
The name Karen is thought to be a reference
to a character from the movie Mean Girls,

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:17.860
but there can also be Mankarens, so this guy
screaming about how killing is “his right”,

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:21.360
and incorrectly citing the name of the group
that gave him that “right” seems be an

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:24.497
almost Simpsonseque prediction of events later
to come.

00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:27.560
Hopefully this isn’t one of those cases
of life imitates art, though.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:31.589
I did find a case of art imitates art, when
the characters make it to Tanya’s house.

00:09:31.589 --> 00:09:35.300
The news coverage they have playing on the
TV is the same channel that James Sandin watched

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.339
a year prior.

00:09:36.339 --> 00:09:39.610
Even though this takes place a year later,
the news scroll at the bottom has the exact

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:43.760
same text as the first movie, about parliament’s
criminal imprisonment measures, and a comedian

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:45.040
copyrighting a catch phrase.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:48.870
Also, it turns out that Shane getting shot
makes Liz realize how much she cares about

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:49.370
him.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:51.160
LIZ: “I'm sorry.”

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:52.188
SHANE: “No, l got shot.”

00:09:52.188 --> 00:09:55.420
LIZ: “Oh, are you gonna use this excuse
for the rest of our lives?”

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:56.317
SHANE: “Well, at least the rest of the night.”

00:09:56.317 --> 00:09:57.193
Well.

00:09:57.193 --> 00:09:59.360
I guess this time they were both right...

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.670
As the group travels through the financial
district, they come across the remains of

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:03.670
a man who has been purged.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.339
There’s a note left on him that says,

00:10:05.339 --> 00:10:07.630
“Here hangs stockbroker David Nuestadter.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:10.990
Stole our pensions now he’s gone.”

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:13.260
However, David Nuestadter is no stockbroker.

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:15.560
He’s a horror film executive producer.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:19.060
In fact, he’s one of the most prolific horror
film producers of the last decade -- he’s

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:22.810
responsible for funding all of the biggest
hits made by Universal Studio’s rival studio

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:23.810
Warner Bros.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:26.029
The spelling of the name is way too specific.

00:10:26.029 --> 00:10:30.019
Clearly, Universal Studios or director James
Demonaco feels that Nuestadter stole something

00:10:30.019 --> 00:10:32.160
from them, and they’re quite bitter about
it.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.940
I’m not sure what that something is… maybe
there were early talks to make The Conjuring

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.600
franchise a Universal / Blumhouse movie before
Neustadter swooped in and secured that $2

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:41.020
billion bag for Warner Bros.

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:44.649
Or maybe Demonaco pitched something to him,
and then one of his future movies was a little

00:10:44.649 --> 00:10:46.160
too similar to his idea.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.350
If anyone knows what this beef might be about,
let me know in the comments.

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:52.519
The climax of the movie would involve our
characters being kidnapped by Godhead and

00:10:52.519 --> 00:10:56.421
his crew and sold off to be victims in this
life-and-death stakes laser tag arena, but

00:10:56.421 --> 00:10:59.849
there’s something interesting about the
soundtrack in this sequence.

00:11:08.858 --> 00:11:13.550
After being kidnapped and sold to rich NFFA
associates who hunt people for sport, the

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:17.461
main group is put on display to be sold off
along with three other victims, and to add

00:11:17.461 --> 00:11:20.959
credibility to Carmelo’s theory, all three
of them are dressed in clothes you’d typically

00:11:20.959 --> 00:11:22.397
see on a homeless person.

00:11:22.397 --> 00:11:24.481
Also, the music being played during this gala

00:11:24.481 --> 00:11:26.585
is a classic piano piece by Chopin.

00:11:26.585 --> 00:11:31.469
Much like how the series opens with a montage of purging set to a classic piece by Debussy.

00:11:31.469 --> 00:11:35.200
After Shane is picked off by one of the bad
guys, speaking of potentially stolen content,

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:38.079
the soundtrack here sounds exactly like a
Green Day song.

00:11:38.079 --> 00:11:51.000
🎵 Slow series of notes from string instrument 🎵

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:58.053
🎵 "21 Guns" - Green Day 🎵
(intro)

00:11:58.053 --> 00:11:59.800
Oh wow, the lyrics fit too!

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:03.480
And that in itself it funny, because 21 Guns
has a melody from...

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:04.680
Full House?

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:05.270
Roll it.

00:12:06.343 --> 00:12:13.300
🎵 "21 Guns" - Green Day 🎵
(solo)

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:17.233
🎵 "Everywhere you look, everywhere you look!" 🎵

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:20.820
So yeah, that’s how The Purge: Anarchy connects
to Full f***ing House

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:22.372
“This is our time now!”

00:12:22.372 --> 00:12:26.230
The team that helps Leo and the others escape
is aided by Dante Bishop from the last movie.

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:28.180
They commandeer a vehicle in the parking lot.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:31.450
At the beginning, Leo was ordering two innocent
people to get out of his car, essentially

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:35.230
leaving them to die in the Purge; but now
he’s ordering two bad people to do the same

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:38.790
-- it’s only been 12 hours, but his experiences
on this night have already started to shape

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:39.790
his morals.

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:42.910
And about 40 minutes later, we see evidence
of his character development again, when he

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:44.959
decides to let his son’s killer go free.

00:12:44.959 --> 00:12:48.600
I guess we don’t technically know that he
was ever planning to kill him, I mean maybe

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:52.639
he was just going to give him a stern talking
to, but most likely, he had malicious intentions,

00:12:52.639 --> 00:12:54.029
but changed his mind.

00:12:54.029 --> 00:12:57.279
After coming out of the house, he’s finally
hunted down by this guy, who’s known as

00:12:57.279 --> 00:12:58.459
Big Daddy.

00:12:58.459 --> 00:12:59.394
Not that Big Daddy.

00:12:59.394 --> 00:13:00.634
Not THAT Big Daddy.

00:13:00.634 --> 00:13:01.634
That Big Daddy.

00:13:01.634 --> 00:13:05.601
It’s here that Barnes learns that the NFFA
interferes with the Purge, and this may have

00:13:05.601 --> 00:13:09.380
been the moment that inspired him to fight
against the NFFA by going into security work

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:12.339
and protecting their political opponents,
as seen in the next movie.

00:13:12.339 --> 00:13:14.699
The final sirens sound, and Leo is rushed
to the hospital.

00:13:14.699 --> 00:13:18.440
I think we now know that this is maybe the
most unrealistic part of The Purge, since

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:22.050
we’ve now seen how bad things can get when
hospitals all reach capacity.

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:25.290
In the credits, there are a few hidden
cameos from the first movie, like the interface

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:28.889
of a Sandin Security system, the group that
broke into the Sandins’ house, and James

00:13:28.889 --> 00:13:29.980
Sandin himself.

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:33.550
At the beginning of this video, I mentioned
how The Purge: Anarchy is a social commentary

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.339
about gun violence in the US.

00:13:35.339 --> 00:13:39.500
Demonaco himself has talked about how it explores
the idea that if there was no government, then

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:40.980
what would dictate our morality?

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:44.230
We see that some people will try to take the
law into their own hands.

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:48.200
We see those without guns of their own being
the most vulnerable targets, but when given

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:51.890
a weapon, they fight violence with violence,
because if you can’t afford one, you can’t

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:55.490
really protect yourself through other means,
the purgers will find you.

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:59.290
It starts with just the gun lovers, but we
see participation in The Purge grow year over

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:02.110
year as the groups being gunned down start
to retaliate.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:06.550
And ultimately, allowing this to go on year
after year causes things to devolve into complete

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:07.790
anarchy.

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:11.750
Click the video on the left for more analysis
of The Purge franchise, and if you love horror

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:15.710
remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring the deathbell for

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:18.810
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:21.200
Assuming we both survive.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.510
If you don’t want to be purged, you should
stay home.

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:25.709
But if you do have to go out there, wear a
mask.

